Add lean SFT commits (bit 20): header-word ACK, Rwrite-only custody

SHELL_FRAME_LEAN_CAPABILITY (1 << 20) is an explicitly required r13 option
on top of terminal-only; both bits must be granted exactly. A complete
frame-submit FrameCommit carries the automatic cumulative ACK bound in its
header sequence word and its exact Rwrite alone settles Custody::Submitted;
a Submitted naming it is a protocol error. The word is confirmed only by the
exact Rwrite, rolled back otherwise, and re-folded on an EAGAIN retry; one
ACK stays in flight. A lone automatic ACK is held 250 ms for the next commit
to carry, with the hold deadline joining wake_deadline. A lean commit may
carry the ACK that covers a retained paired Open. The protocol codec accepts
a nonzero sequence word only on a FrameCommit candidate. Open, Close and
paired submissions are unchanged. Spec copy of the wire contract updated;
API-PARITY records the C comparison.
